{"timestamp":"2026-05-07T00:09:17.428Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The better fix is to stop relying on per-line `nolint` in [tui_model.go](/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/feat/entire-migrate-lock/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go:111).\n\nWhat’s happening: `mise run lint:go` runs `golangci-lint run --fix ./...`, and `nolintlint` is auto-fixable. If a `//nolint:ireturn` is considered unused or redundant under the current config, the fixer can delete it. That makes these comments a bad long-term guardrail.\n\nBest options:\n\n1. **Project-level allow for Bubble Tea**\n   Add `charm.land/bubbletea/v2.Model` to `.golangci.yaml` under `linters.settings.ireturn.allow`.\n\n   That says: returning `tea.Model` is allowed because Bubble Tea requires it. Then we can remove `//nolint:ireturn` from all Bubble Tea `Update` methods instead of fighting the fixer.\n\n2. **Local refactor for helpers**\n   Change internal helpers like `handleAgentEvent` and `handleKey` to return `reviewTUIModel, tea.Cmd` instead of `tea.Model, tea.Cmd`. Only `Update` actually needs Bubble Tea’s interface return.\n\n   This reduces the surface area, but `Update` still needs either a config allow or an exclusion.\n\n3. **Path-specific lint exclusion**\n   Add an `ireturn` exclusion for `cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go`.\n\n   I’d avoid this unless we want review TUI to be special. The framework-level allow is cleaner because this pattern appears in other TUI files too.\n\nMy recommendation: add `charm.land/bubbletea/v2.Model` to the `ireturn.allow` list and then remove these `nolint:ireturn` comments across Bubble Tea models. That turns this from comment churn into an explicit lint policy.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
